# Swift/iOS testing

Narrows `core-common-rules`' testing rules to Swift Testing (default for new test code) and legacy XCTest where the project has not migrated.

## Swift Testing vs XCTest

- For new tests on a toolchain that supports it, prefer Swift Testing
  (`import Testing`, `@Test`, `#expect`/`#require`) over XCTest.
- `XCUITest` and performance tests (`XCTMetric`/`measure`) stay on XCTest; an
  existing XCTest suite is not rewritten wholesale, and the two coexist in one
  target. Match the target's existing framework per kind of test; add Swift
  Testing for new unit tests, without mixing conventions within one file.
- A Swift Testing function is `@Test func name() async throws { ... }`: no
  `test` prefix, no `XCTestCase` subclass. `#expect(condition)` records a failure
  and continues; `try #require(optional)` stops the test.

## Structure and naming

- One `@Test` (or XCTest method) per behavior, with a descriptive name
  (`@Test("returns nil for an empty cart")` or `test_returnsNil_whenCartIsEmpty`).
- Use `arguments:` parameterization for the same assertion over several inputs,
  not a hand-rolled loop or copy-pasted tests.
- Group with a `struct`/`enum` namespace and `@Suite`, or an `XCTestCase`
  subclass for legacy code, matching the target.

## Mocking at the protocol boundary

- Mock external dependencies (network clients, persistence, platform services) at
  a protocol boundary production code already depends on, never the type under
  test's internal collaborators or private state.
- Define or reuse a narrow protocol (`protocol OrderClient { func fetchOrder(id: String) async throws -> Order }`),
  inject the real type in production and a test double in tests.
- Do not mock one layer too deep (a private helper, or a concrete `URLSession`
  call instead of the protocol that wraps it).

## Async and concurrency in tests

- Mark the test `async` and `await` the call directly; no `XCTestExpectation` or
  semaphore to bridge an `async` API unless the minimum toolchain predates async tests.
- Never synchronize with a fixed delay (`Thread.sleep`/`Task.sleep` as a guess);
  `await` the call, join a `TaskGroup`, or await an `XCTestExpectation` with a
  real fulfillment signal.
- Annotate a test `@MainActor` when it exercises `@MainActor`-isolated
  view-model/state code.

## Determinism

- No dependence on real network access, the real Keychain or wall-clock time;
  inject a fake at the protocol boundary and a clock/date provider instead of
  calling `Date()` in the code under test.
- A bug fix gets a regression test that fails before the fix and passes after;
  new behavior gets coverage in the same change.
